--- 2. Scale out 2 -> 10, sampling availability throughout (paced under the rate limit)
    responses during scale-out: 200 200 200 200 200 200 200 200 200 200 200 200 200 200 
    reached 10 replicas in 10s
    READY=10/10  UP-TO-DATE=10  AVAILABLE=10
    Pending pods: 0

--- 3. What the scheduler had to reserve
      Resource           Requests      Limits
      cpu                1100m (55%)   5100m (254%)
      memory             1228Mi (15%)  3626Mi (45%)
    NOTE: replicas are bounded by one node's allocatable capacity. Horizontal scaling here
    buys concurrency and rollout safety, not fault tolerance: all 10 replicas share the
    single node, so this does not address the single point of failure.

